(132, 132, 4, 4, 4, 4, 3, 4, 3, 3, 3, 4, 3, 2, 2, 'He is a beginner, therefore he\'s still getting comfortable with the ball. Softer touches would be more beneficial over kicking the ball ', 'He kicks the ball most of the time, even in situations when he has space and time to control the ball ', 'As a beginner and one of the youngest in the group, most passes are too heavy from his teammates so he doesn\'t control them well. He does better with passes from coaching because his limitations are put into consideration ', 'He needs to take softer touches to change direction better ', 'His accuracy is decent for his size &  age however he kicks the with his laces without supervision. He is improving with his in foot technique when he\'s reminded  ', 'He hasn\'t attempted long range passing ', 'He needs to take softer touches instead of kicking the ball and running behind the ball ', 'He is comfortable with the ball against opponents of a similar size. He can improve with softer touches and change in direction ', 'He shoots with his laces. His shooting power is good enough for his age & size, however he can improve with shooting while the ball is moving ', 'I haven\'t asked him to or seen him attempt headers. He will need more practice as he grows', 'He gives everything to retrieve the ball when asked to. He puts in effort against bigger and older players, he gets results against his pairs ', 'He\'s a baller. Follows instructions & makes adjustments ', 'He is as fast/quick as anyone in his age range ', 'He is one of the youngest \r\nHe displays supermassive potential \r\nHe should keep playing at his level till he grows/developes into a leadership role where he can/will be one of the best in his age group '),
(133, 133, 4, 3, 3, 4, 3, 4, 4, 3, 2, 4, 3, 2, 4, 'He tends to shy away from taking many touches on the ball.', 'He receives the ball and keeps it under control. With time this technique will improve', 'Usually, the ball gets stuck in his feet, he does keep it under control but needs improvement on his consistency of first touch in open space', 'Needs to turn with the ball faster. In his age group this a technique that develops over time', 'He passes the ball well in a short range distance. Needs to pass more with his in-foot', 'Needs to improve his long-range passing ability', 'He\'s shy of taking many touches and usually always looks to pass or shoot the first time', '1v1 ability is not bad. Will improve with continuous training', 'Shoots well and keeps his shot on target and low with good enough power', 'This is a technique that takes time to develop when he goes up the age groups', 'He\'s not a soft tackler but will improve on his timing of tackles and interceptions', 'Good motor skills, good arm-to-leg coordination and good balance, which help him improve his football ability', 'Needs to improve moving the ball quicker', 'Devansh has a good shooting ability which is his strength and needs to keep improving on this ability. He needs to improve on his dribbling and running with the ball technique to add to his game. Devansh is a fun character to coach, he is attentive when he has to be, he has the willingness to learn and remembers coaching points'),
(134, 134, 3, 3, 2, 3, 2, 4, 3, 3, 3, 4, 2, 4, 4, 'His ball mastery and manipulation of the ball is good when he puts in the effort and doesn\'t just kick the ball', 'He receives the ball well on his dominant foot', 'His first touch is good because he keeps the balls under control and close to him', 'He kicks the ball and runs behind it over taking soft touches ', 'His short passes are decent with his in-foot', 'I haven\'t seen him pass long range as most of his drills/assignments haven\'t been long range ', 'He takes a touch with every step when reminded', 'He keeps the ball & dribbles decently in 1v1 situations ', 'He has decent shooting power and accuracy ', 'He needs to work on and improve on his heading ', 'He is good at identifying targets and disposing the opposition ', 'He doesn\'t put the required effort into SAQ\'s', 'He needs to improve his speed', 'He performs when he puts in the effort. He needs to be active and engaged throughout his sessions '),
